# Secrets. .env.example is the committed template; anything with real values
# stays out of the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The Android app's signing key, its passwords, and Firebase's files, wherever
# they end up. android/.gitignore covers its own folder; these catch a key
# saved anywhere else in the repository by mistake.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
keystore.properties
google-services.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json

# release/<version>/ keeps the Android builds (release/README.md): the APK and the App Bundle for
# Google Play, and this README. GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB, so one that big is listed here
# by name and goes only on the GitHub release (none so far). The rest never goes in git: the
# desktop installers (GitHub Actions puts them on the release), their latest*.yml files, and the
# R8 mapping and Dart symbols that read crash reports back, which stay on this computer.
release/**
!release/*/
!release/README.md
!release/*/*.apk
!release/*/*.aab
release/*/*-mapping.txt
release/*/*-symbols.zip

# The desktop installers, wherever else a build leaves them.
*.deb
*.AppImage
*.msi
*.dmg
*-setup.exe

# What's left on disk of the Capacitor app (1.0.x), which flutter/ replaced: its keystore copy,
# Firebase file, builds and packages. Never committed.
/android/

# Vercel
.vercel

# Local tooling
node_modules/
*.log

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
